### Square root sqrt(me) via DD. Crashes on a non-finite result (me<0).
### :returns: The square root of `me`.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} on NaN (me<0); {NumericOverflowError} on ±inf.
routine D64.sqrt!() -> D64
  var r = me.sqrt_unchecked()
  if r.is_finite()
    return r
  if r.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

### sqrt(me), raw IEEE: NaN for me<0. Never crashes.
### :returns: The square root of `me`, possibly NaN.
routine D64.sqrt_unchecked() -> D64
  # DD.sqrt clamps every non-positive input to 0; preserve IEEE by mapping a strictly
  # negative operand to NaN (me<0) while a signed zero still yields +0 through DD.sqrt.
  if me.is_negative() and not me.is_zero()
    return D64.quiet_nan()
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).sqrt_unchecked())

### Cube root cbrt(me) via DD (defined for all reals). Never crashes.
### :returns: The cube root of `me`.
routine D64.cbrt() -> D64
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).cbrt())

### me^you (general power) via DD, raw IEEE: may return ±inf or NaN. Never crashes.
### :param you: The exponent.
### :returns: `me` raised to the power `you`, possibly non-finite.
routine D64.pow_unchecked(you: D64) -> D64
  # DD.pow computes exp(you * ln|me|) — the general POSITIVE-base power. A negative base is
  # only real for an integer exponent: restore the magnitude via |me|^you and set the sign
  # from the exponent's parity (odd -> negative); a non-integer exponent is a domain NaN.
  var r = f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me.abs()).pow_unchecked(you: d64_to_f128(x: you)))
  if not (me.is_negative() and not me.is_zero())
    return r
  var yint = you.trunc()
  if you.cmp(you: yint) isnot SAME
    return D64.quiet_nan()
  # parity: yint - 2*trunc(yint/2) is 0 (even) or ±1 (odd)
  var parity = yint - D64(from: 2_s64) * (yint / D64(from: 2_s64)).trunc()
  if parity.is_zero()
    return r
  return r.neg()

### sqrt(x^2 + y^2) (without spurious overflow) via DD. Crashes if non-finite.
### :param x: The first leg.
### :param y: The second leg.
### :returns: The Euclidean length `hypot(x, y)`.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} when the result is NaN; {NumericOverflowError} on ±inf.
routine hypot!(x: D64, y: D64) -> D64
  var r = hypot_unchecked(x: x, y: y)
  if r.is_finite()
    return r
  if r.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

### `hypot(x, y)`, raw IEEE: may return +inf. Never crashes.
### :param x: The first leg.
### :param y: The second leg.
### :returns: The Euclidean length, possibly +inf.
routine hypot_unchecked(x: D64, y: D64) -> D64
  return f128_to_d64(x: hypot_unchecked(x: d64_to_f128(x: x), y: d64_to_f128(x: y)))

### Fused multiply-add me*b + c, single rounding, via DD. Crashes if non-finite.
### :param b: The multiplier.
### :param c: The addend.
### :returns: `me * b + c` rounded once.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} when the result is NaN; {NumericOverflowError} on ±inf.
routine D64.fma!(b: D64, c: D64) -> D64
  var r = me.fma_unchecked(b: b, c: c)
  if r.is_finite()
    return r
  if r.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

### `me * b + c` (single rounding), raw IEEE: may return ±inf or NaN. Never crashes.
### :param b: The multiplier.
### :param c: The addend.
### :returns: `me * b + c`, possibly non-finite.
routine D64.fma_unchecked(b: D64, c: D64) -> D64
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).fma_unchecked(b: d64_to_f128(x: b), c: d64_to_f128(x: c)))

### Sine sin(me) (radians) via DD. Never crashes (NaN for non-finite input).
### :returns: The sine of `me`.
routine D64.sin() -> D64
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).sin())

### Cosine cos(me) (radians) via DD. Never crashes (NaN for non-finite input).
### :returns: The cosine of `me`.
routine D64.cos() -> D64
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).cos())

### Tangent tan(me) (radians) via DD. Never crashes (NaN for non-finite input).
### :returns: The tangent of `me`.
routine D64.tan() -> D64
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).tan())

### Arcsine asin(me) via DD. Crashes if non-finite (|me|>1).
### :returns: The arcsine of `me` in radians.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} on NaN (|me|>1); {NumericOverflowError} on ±inf.
routine D64.asin!() -> D64
  var r = me.asin_unchecked()
  if r.is_finite()
    return r
  if r.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

### asin(me), raw IEEE: NaN for |me|>1. Never crashes.
### :returns: The arcsine of `me`, possibly NaN.
routine D64.asin_unchecked() -> D64
  # DD.asin = atan(me/sqrt(1-me^2)); for |me|>1 that sqrt clamps to 0 (wrong ±pi/2 instead of
  # NaN), so guard the domain here to preserve IEEE (asin NaN for |me|>1).
  if me.abs().cmp(you: D64(from: 1_s64)) is ME_LARGE
    return D64.quiet_nan()
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).asin_unchecked())

### Arccosine acos(me) via DD. Crashes if non-finite (|me|>1).
### :returns: The arccosine of `me` in radians.
### :throws: {NumericDomainError} on NaN (|me|>1); {NumericOverflowError} on ±inf.
routine D64.acos!() -> D64
  var r = me.acos_unchecked()
  if r.is_finite()
    return r
  if r.is_nan()
    throw NumericDomainError(description: "domain error: no real result")
  throw NumericOverflowError(description: "overflow: out of range")

### acos(me), raw IEEE: NaN for |me|>1. Never crashes.
### :returns: The arccosine of `me`, possibly NaN.
routine D64.acos_unchecked() -> D64
  # acos = pi/2 - asin; same |me|>1 domain guard (DD.sqrt clamp would otherwise mask the NaN).
  if me.abs().cmp(you: D64(from: 1_s64)) is ME_LARGE
    return D64.quiet_nan()
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).acos_unchecked())

### Arctangent atan(me) via DD (defined for all reals). Never crashes.
### :returns: The arctangent of `me` in radians.
routine D64.atan() -> D64
  return f128_to_d64(x: d64_to_f128(x: me).atan())

### Two-argument arctangent atan2(y, x), quadrant-aware, via DD. Never crashes.
### :param y: The y-coordinate.
### :param x: The x-coordinate.
### :returns: The angle of (x, y) in radians, in (-pi, pi].
routine atan2(y: D64, x: D64) -> D64
  return f128_to_d64(x: atan2(y: d64_to_f128(x: y), x: d64_to_f128(x: x)))

### Hyperbolic sine sinh(me) via DD. Crashes if non-finite (overflow for large |me|).
